# Build context for Dockerfile.marketing: the Astro project in site/ plus
# repo markdown read at build time for /privacy/, /changelog/ and /docs/.
# Ignore everything, then re-include the site sources and those files.
*
!site/
!Dockerfile.marketing
!PRIVACY.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!README.md
!docs/
docs/**
!docs/sync-setup.md
!docs/kanban-format.md
!docs/a11y-checklist.md
!docs/sync-safety.md
# Local build output and tooling never enter the context (the image runs npm ci itself).
site/node_modules
site/dist
site/.astro
site/.proof-w1
site/.proof-w3
site/.proof-w7

# Build context for Dockerfile.web: the wasm bundle is compiled from source
# inside the image, so the workspace, the pinned toolchain, the Rune font and
# sample-vault assets, the vendored crates patches, the build script and the
# nginx config all join the context. target/ stays out: web-build.sh writes it
# inside the image, and the host's copy is never needed.
!Dockerfile.web
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!crates/
!xtask/
!vendor/
!assets/
!vault/
!scripts/
!web/
